  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Acceleration of Malaria Elimination in Indonesia - Indonesia (01-Jan-2024-31-Dec-2026)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Indonesia, Malaria, Persatuan Karya Dharma Kesehatan Indonesia (also known as &#x201c;PERDHAKI&#x201d;, Association of Voluntary Health Services of Indonesia) (PERDHAKI)This program has the following goals: 86% of the Indonesian territory is free of malaria transmission, and no district with annual parasite incidence (API) &gt; 1 per 1000 at-risk populations by the end of 2026.. The objectives of this program are: Increased in number of malaria-free districts from 347 districts in 2022 to 445 districts in 2026..  Achieved positivity rate for Papua province (along with the newly created province) &lt;5% by the end of 2026..  Malaria elimination status is maintained in districts determined to achieve malaria elimination.</narrative>
  </description>
